# Network Policy Demo

This folder shows how Kubernetes network policies restrict traffic between pods and namespaces.

## What it does

The policy allows inbound traffic only from pods in the `access` namespace or from pods with the label `access=true` on TCP port 80.

This demonstrates how to isolate workloads and control which traffic is allowed into a namespace.

## Example purpose

- restrict pod-to-pod communication
- allow only trusted namespaces to reach an app
- demonstrate ingress filtering in Kubernetes
